{"t": 1794107536.333482, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s \u2014 root cause found. Upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row, but reports/export.py wrote CSV with a hard-coded fieldnames=[\"id\", \"amount\"]. csv.DictWriter raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` on every export (4,120 occurrences in CloudWatch /ecs/reports-api, eu-west-1), so the API failed all report requests and the gateway returned 502. Fix: added `currency` to the export fieldnames (id,amount,currency); verified locally that rows now export cleanly. Needs a deploy of reports-api to take effect."}, "ok": true}
